; Canonical Atomic<T> operations. xa_intrinsic_id distinguishes individual
; RMW semantics (add/sub/fetch/swap/CAS/toggle) without a method-name payload.
;
; The :sync column declares the strongest happens-before edge the op can carry
; (spec §16.9.2, contracts/memory-model.md). The user picks the actual order at
; run time via the `Ordering` argument, so the static declaration is the
; fail-closed upper bound: an acquire load must keep later memory operations
; from moving above it even when the argument turns out to be Relaxed, because
; the argument is not always a compile-time constant.
