;; `stored-value` means "arg 0 is the container, arg 1+ is the value", which is
;; the shape of xi.store.field. This op is arity 1 — the upvalue index lives in
;; aux, so the value IS arg 0 — and under `stored-value` arg 0 read as the
;; container and was never treated as consumed. ARC then released a value the
;; cell had just taken ownership of, so `h = Child(2)` inside a closure left the
;; enclosing frame reading freed memory.
(define-xi-op xi.store.upval
